---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import VideoGrid from '../components/VideoGrid.astro';

// Runtime in each category so nobody clicks a 10-minute film expecting a
// sizzle reel. Destination work is in scope per the hero copy.
// No "Coming soon" tiles: two real films beat three tiles where one is empty.
// Ordered so the two Parker and Andrew pieces sit together: the same wedding as
// a 38-second sizzle and as the full 8-minute film. That pairing IS the offer,
// and it is the through-line the whole site runs on: the complete record plus
// the short piece you can actually use.
// Couples are NOT named here, by Geoff's decision (2026-07-31). Films are
// labelled purely by what they are, and ordered to alternate sizzle / full
// film / sizzle / full film, so the grid reads as a catalogue of the two
// deliverables rather than four unrelated clips. Runtimes do the distinguishing.
const videos = [
  { title: 'Sizzle reel', category: 'Wedding · 38 sec', vimeo: '1150766730' },
  { title: 'Full wedding film', category: 'Wedding · 8 min', vimeo: '1214642067' },
  { title: 'Sizzle reel', category: 'Wedding · 37 sec', vimeo: '1214638739' },
  { title: 'Full wedding film', category: 'Destination · Hawaii, 10 min', vimeo: '1067969852' },
];

// PRICING is real and confirmed by Geoff 2026-07-29, with elopement and
// destination added 2026-08-07 from the retired Pixieset site and re-confirmed
// by him. Keep it accurate or remove it; a stale price is worse than no price.
//   Elopement ........................... $2,000  (shorter day, shorter edit)
//   Destination ......................... $3,500  plus flights and hotel at cost
//   All-day coverage, one shooter ....... $3,500
//   Second shooter ...................... +$500
//   Included: full-length wedding highlight film
//   Ceremony edit ....................... $800
//   Toasts edit ......................... $600
//   Ceremony + toasts together .......... $1,000
//   Sizzle reel ......................... $200
//   Coverage ends when the couple leaves
//   Delivery: 6 to 8 weeks
//
// NOTE ON POSITIONING: the old headline claimed "Eight weddings a year", which
// was an arbitrary number, not a policy. Geoff shoots 3 this year, used to do
// 8 to 12, and is deliberately shifting focus toward corporate work. So this
// page no longer states a count, and it no longer pretends scarcity is the
// selling point. Selectivity is real; the specific number was not.

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Wedding Videography',
  description: 'Cinematic wedding films with all-day coverage, including a full-length highlight film.',
  url: 'https://sdubmedia.com/weddings',
  serviceType: 'Wedding Videography',
  provider: { '@type': 'LocalBusiness', '@id': 'https://sdubmedia.com/#business', name: 'SDub Media' },
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Nashville' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Nolensville' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Franklin' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Brentwood' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Murfreesboro' },
  ],
  hasOfferCatalog: {
    '@type': 'OfferCatalog',
    name: 'Wedding Videography',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Elopement', price: '2000', priceCurrency: 'USD', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock' },
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'All-day coverage', price: '3500', priceCurrency: 'USD', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock' },
    ],
  },
};
---
<Layout
  title="Nashville Wedding Videographer | SDub Media"
  description="Cinematic wedding films in Nashville and beyond. Elopements $2,000, all-day coverage $3,500 including a full-length highlight film. Clear pricing, 6 to 8 week delivery."

  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">Weddings</span>
    <h1>A few weddings a year.<br>Every one deliberate.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">Most of our work is for businesses, which is why the weddings we take are unhurried. A small number, all day, and never edited between three other jobs.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Check availability</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  {/* Every image on this page is a frame pulled from an actual wedding film,
      not a posed photo. That is the point: it shows a couple what the footage
      itself looks like. Sized 1600px wide, ~250KB each. */}
  <div class="container" style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
    <img class="wedding-hero-img" src="/images/weddings/sunset-carry.jpg"
         alt="A groom lifting his bride mid-kiss as the sun sets behind an open field"
         width="1600" height="900" />
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What it costs</span>
      <h2>The whole day, and the film you will still be watching in ten years.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Almost every wedding videographer makes you email to find out if they are even in your range. We would rather just tell you.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span><strong>Elopement</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">A shorter day and a shorter edit, for an intimate celebration</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$2,000</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
        <span><strong>All-day coverage</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">One shooter, including your full-length highlight film</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$3,500</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span><strong>Destination</strong><br><span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">The same all-day coverage, plus flights and hotel at cost</span></span>
        <span style="white-space: nowrap;"><strong>$3,500</strong> plus travel</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span>Second shooter</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;">$500</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span>Full ceremony edit</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;">$800</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span>Toasts edit</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;">$600</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <span>Ceremony and toasts together</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;">$1,000</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem;">
        <span>Sizzle reel</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;">$200</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">We take only a handful of weddings a year. That does mean the good dates go early.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{/* Portraits moved to /photography (Aug 2026). They were half this page while
    the nav said "Weddings", and a couple comparing wedding films does not want
    to scroll past family sessions to reach the pricing. What is left is a
    pointer, so the work is still reachable from here. */}
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Also</span>
      <h2>We photograph as well as film.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Family sessions, senior portraits, headshots and listings all live on the <a href="/photography">photography page</a>, with pricing and recent work.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How the day works</span>
      <h2>All day means all day.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/weddings/reception-dusk.jpg" alt="A beachside wedding reception under string lights after sunset" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
        <h3>We Leave When You Leave</h3>
        <p>No hour packages, no clock-watching at the reception. Morning through the end of the night. The last hour is often the best footage of the day, and it is the one most packages cut off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/weddings/bridge-kiss.jpg" alt="A couple kissing on a bridge, the bride's veil and train spread behind her" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
        <h3>The Highlight Film Is Included</h3>
        <p>It comes with the booking, not as an upgrade. Ceremony and toasts are separate because not every couple wants them, and charging everyone would be dishonest pricing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/weddings/rings-detail.jpg" alt="Wedding rings resting among white daisies in the bouquet" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
        <h3>Six to Eight Weeks</h3>
        <p>The real timeline, not a hopeful one. We would rather say eight weeks and deliver than promise three and go quiet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">A few of the days</span>
      <h2>Three weddings, three completely different days.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="wedding-strip">
      <img src="/images/weddings/wedding-party.jpg" alt="A wedding party posed together on a lakeside deck beneath a floral arch" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
      <img src="/images/weddings/autumn-field.jpg" alt="A couple holding hands in a tall autumn field under a clear sky" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
      <img src="/images/weddings/bride-bridge.jpg" alt="A bride walking across a wooden bridge holding a bouquet of daisies" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
      <img src="/images/weddings/barn-pond.jpg" alt="A couple kissing beside a pond, their reflection in the water and a timber barn venue behind" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who shoots it</span>
      <h2>Specialists, not one person with a camera.</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">A wedding is the least repeatable thing we film, so it is the owner on the camera, every time.</p>
    {/* Roles only, never names or faces: the team is not willing to appear on
        the marketing site and that stays their call. These are the confirmed
        roles (see /about). Do not add one to fill a page. */}
    <ul class="facts" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <li>The <strong>owner</strong> shoots every wedding the company takes, which is part of why we take so few</li>
      <li>A <strong>second shooter</strong> when you add one, so the aisle and the faces are covered at the same moment</li>
      <li><strong>Editing in house</strong>, so your film is not waiting behind somebody else's queue</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">More on <a href="/about">who shows up</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Watch a film</span>
      <h2>What you actually receive.</h2>
    </div>
    <VideoGrid items={videos} center />
    <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 2.5rem; color: var(--muted);">Nashville, destination, or wherever you are celebrating. <a href="/contact">Check availability</a> and we will tell you straight away whether the date is open.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
